---
description: Keep project documentation synchronized with every behavior or workflow change
alwaysApply: true
---

# Documentation is part of the change

- Read `docs/MAINTENANCE.md` before changing behavior, setup, architecture,
  model contracts, platform support, or release operations.
- Update the relevant README and detailed docs in the same change.
- Keep `docs/BEGINNER_GUIDE.md`, `docs/GETTING_STARTED.md`, and
  `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md` accurate for first-time contributors.
- Update `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` when data flow, trust boundaries, storage,
  routing, model I/O, or inference changes.
- Update `apps/web/README.md` and `apps/web/vercel.json` for web deploy changes.
- Update `tools/model/README.md`, `tools/model/RELEASE.md`, and
  `tools/model/.env.example` for export, signing, R2, env names, release, or
  rollback changes.
- Update `apps/native/README.md`, platform notes, and
  `apps/native/docs/PRIVACY.md` for Flutter, native, or privacy-promise
  changes.
- Document observed behavior and explicit limitations; do not claim model
  accuracy without representative fixture results.
- Never include tokens, private keys, R2 credentials, transcripts, or audio in
  documentation or examples.
- Verify commands, paths, local links, tests, and builds before handing off.
